  "notes": "Curriculum guide as printed in the 2023-2024 ASU Undergraduate Catalog (Dept. of English, Languages and Mass Communication). 120-hour curriculum: 36 hours general education (incl. CO 100, CO 103, SA 223); 9 hours upper-level free electives; 57 hours required upper-level Mass Communications courses; 18 hours upper-level electives in Mass Communications, Sports Management, Business, Marketing and Physical Education (incl. CO 344, SM 200, SM 201, MK 325, PE 327, SM 401 or BA 439). To be eligible for graduation, all students must earn a C or above in all required elective courses and pass a Senior Exit Examination. *Or other approved Social Science course.",
